0..77 Comment "// A ring buffer held other than exactly once. The kernel owns a buffer while"
78..152 Comment "// an operation is in flight and hands it back with the completion (boats,"
153..228 Comment "// _Notes on io-uring_, 2020): a buffer never handed back leaks its slot in"
229..304 Comment "// the registered area, one handed back twice is reclaimed while the kernel"
305..380 Comment "// may still own it, and one read while held would observe bytes the kernel"
381..405 Comment "// may still be writing."
407..450 Comment "// The native buffer a receive places live."
